course: dictionary
lesson: 19
title: Abroad: other countries
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Abroad means in or to a foreign country, a country that is not your own. You can go abroad, live abroad or travel abroad. «Families go abroad on holiday» tells you they travel to another country for a break.
explain: Look for clues around the word. Here the clues are holiday and a trip to another country. In «Clothes ... are shipped abroad to markets», the word shipped tells you the clothes are sent by boat to markets in other countries.
explain: «From abroad» means coming from another country. To check your meaning, swap in your own words: «a visitor from abroad» becomes «a visitor from a foreign country». If the sentence still makes sense, your meaning is right.
fact: «Abroad» means in or to a foreign country, one that is not your own.
fact: In «go abroad» and «live abroad», abroad works as an adverb. In «from abroad», the phrase names a place, so it is used like a noun.
fact: «From abroad» means coming from another country.
fact: When you travel abroad, stay close to an adult, know the name of your hotel, and learn the local emergency number.
fact: The phrase «at home and abroad» means in your own country and in other countries.
exercise: «Almost all giant pandas in zoos abroad are lent by China.» What does abroad mean here? | Inside a big cage | At the top of a tree | In the same town as the zoo | *In other countries, not your own
exercise: Lily's cousin is a visitor from abroad. What does from abroad mean? | Coming from the next street | Coming from the sea | Coming from the shop | *Coming from another country
exercise: Your family is going abroad for a holiday. What should you do when you travel abroad? | Wander off alone to find new friends | Ignore the local emergency number | Leave your passport on the bus | *Stay close to an adult and know your hotel's name
test: «Families go abroad on holiday.» What does abroad mean here? | Very quickly | *In or to another country | Under the sea | In the garden
test: Which word means in or to a foreign country? | Curt | Barely | Glum | *Abroad
exam: Which sentence uses abroad correctly? | The abroad ran fast across the field | We went abroad the shop for milk | *We hope to live abroad when we are older | Abroad the dog is very happy today
